{"title":"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_(Solution_1_Simplified)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (Solution 1 Simplified)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(3_degree_polynominal_graph)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (3 degree polynominal graph)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> does the expression<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb19417f3c2ddfd1ca85657b18676af13834b8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{\\log (n^2) - (\\log n)^2}{\\log n - 3}}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"53\" />represent a real number, where log denotes the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> logarithm?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/0/b00e4096a0cebd0aaabb1964b184bc455463fc4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }900 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }3\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }902 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 2  \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }901$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"410\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/073617256cc5838f5661837cf20805753f2b8747.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sqrt{\\frac{\\log \\left( n^2 \\right) - \\left( \\log n \\right)^2}{\\log n - 3}} &amp; = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\log n - \\left( \\log n \\right)^2}{\\log n - 3}} \\\\ &amp; = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\left( \\log n \\right) \\left( 2 - \\log n\\right)}{\\log n - 3}} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"347\" height=\"114\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8ef5d99b6283c2870a6ee57f083ca8c96c374c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> is well defined, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be a positive integer.\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db61fd75a1a8bb6fa2b202b6b73daf9b4c9838d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The above expression is 0. So these are valid solutions.\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8408a7f9ca98cf2d36524bac22b032866236cb6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\neq 1, 10^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a79c76c50d9c342237f39e46ffce87d4413c33b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa26366bd3015ac1a1f384ebbf1c90555177f5e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 - \\log n \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />.\nTo make the above expression real, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b673f2ace324243dfadbfde5e6897534134a8adf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 &lt; \\log n &lt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />.\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e447545273a28c36bfa4fe651e224c02bb438a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 &lt; n &lt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" />.\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41aa88d54b8d8a4ff507e435281b49c261b033a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101 \\leq n \\leq 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />.\nHence, the number of solutions in this case is 899.\n</p><p>Putting all cases together, the total number of solutions is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4bfc0c3ef97b5944b712355909a91951aeed651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) 901}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28Solution_1_Simplified.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(Solution_1_Simplified)\">Solution (Solution 1 Simplified)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (Solution 1 Simplified)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572bb806e5a8813ebc476198054a28b4b504864f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(n^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"21\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a23e5458e680b4dfc7f61735ee43ec2c320c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\log(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/75099c3650a888573696ac8a5b95c712d93b37c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\log(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />, the equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/540c24023528cf8dd35b4fc8dccb4b6730ef7450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{2a-a^2}{a-3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"82\" height=\"45\" /> which can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd78fd2ddd93387dbb912247a863cf4c349402b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{a(2-a)}{a-3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"88\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/761f953f34c7f838cd0742690928b86e9710a5ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />\nThe expression is undefined when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340605c5f88cf6864adc5b146c3dffca7a45df22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc53b0797a12d17273b1496cdffc030ef0a77bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, it is trivial to see that the denominator is positive and the numerator is negative, thus resulting in no real solutions.\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e9945b408b30158cc68987e6509cb660767e865d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le a&lt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, the numerator is zero, giving us a valid solution. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/9595e75b87fc7454d6ebed7496c7515708441f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, both the denominator and numerator are negative so all real values of a in this interval is a solution to the equation. All integers of n that makes this true are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db61fd75a1a8bb6fa2b202b6b73daf9b4c9838d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/3/603855e6c3f154c2ddf711702e00ddfdb9dc1dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^3-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. There are 900 solutions here. \n</p><p>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/32168374aa4aff997b6da10714250163321a297a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a&lt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />\nThe numerator will be positive but the denominator is negative, no real solutions exist. \n</p><p>Case 4: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />\nThe expression evaluates to zero, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> valid solution exists. \n</p><p>Case 5: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8362e1f78725beb1de44c30360f0a10d0d3c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />\nAll values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8362e1f78725beb1de44c30360f0a10d0d3c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7131a511be8e37bfc0c54c84ca0c4c1f3e3cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;n&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, no integer solutions exist. \n</p><p>Adding up the cases:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab4012ce9900f7db2e11b3a67a5786eb2bcf696c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900+1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) 901}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"158\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~woeIsMe\ntypesetting: paras\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.283_degree_polynominal_graph.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(3_degree_polynominal_graph)\">Solution 3 (3 degree polynominal graph)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (3 degree polynominal graph)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f63bb98e0feb7f9ba88fb5c70607cd804f60bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a(2-a)}{a-3} &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"104\" height=\"42\" /> , \n</p><p>transform it into a(a-2)(a-3) &lt;0 , \n</p><p>use the following graph to quickly confirm \n</p><p>1) a &lt; 0 or\n</p><p>2) 2 &lt; a &lt;3\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2023_AMC12B_P7.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f2/2023_AMC12B_P7.PNG/600px-2023_AMC12B_P7.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"309\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f2/2023_AMC12B_P7.PNG/900px-2023_AMC12B_P7.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/f2/2023_AMC12B_P7.PNG 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GGdJJzzbivM\">https://youtu.be/GGdJJzzbivM</a>\n</p><p><br />\n~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B\">2023 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235010\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.082 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 294/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2294/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7202/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.881      1 -total\n 58.01%    8.052      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 40.44%    5.613      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-